{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_009","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"Note: This feature is available in Web Workers .","location_hint":"paragraph 138","char_start":2731,"char_end":2779,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_010","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"WebGL (Web Graphics Library) is a JavaScript API for rendering high-performance interactive 3D and 2D graphics within any compatible web browser without the use of plug-ins. WebGL does so by introducing an API that closely conforms to OpenGL ES 2.0 that can be used in HTML <canvas> elements. This conformance makes it possible for the API to take advantage of hardware graphics acceleration provided by the user's device.","location_hint":"paragraph 139","char_start":2781,"char_end":3203,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_011","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"Support for WebGL is present in all modern browsers (see the compatibility tables below); however, the user's device must also have hardware that supports these features.","location_hint":"paragraph 140","char_start":3205,"char_end":3375,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_012","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"The WebGL 2 API introduces support for much of the OpenGL ES 3.0 feature set; it's provided through the WebGL2RenderingContext interface.","location_hint":"paragraph 141","char_start":3377,"char_end":3514,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_013","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"The <canvas> element is also used by the Canvas API to do 2D graphics on web pages.","location_hint":"paragraph 142","char_start":3516,"char_end":3599,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_014","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"EXT_texture_filter_anisotropic","location_hint":"paragraph 181","char_start":4356,"char_end":4386,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
