{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_016","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"WEBGL_compressed_texture_s3tc_srgb","location_hint":"paragraph 200","char_start":4858,"char_end":4892,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_017","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"WebGL 2 is a major update to WebGL which is provided through the WebGL2RenderingContext interface. It is based on OpenGL ES 3.0 and new features include:","location_hint":"paragraph 215","char_start":5180,"char_end":5333,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_018","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"Promoted extensions that are now core to WebGL 2: Vertex Array objects , instancing , multiple render targets , fragment depth .","location_hint":"paragraph 222","char_start":5460,"char_end":5588,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
