{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_046","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"Enable JavaScript to view this browser compatibility table.","location_hint":"paragraph 271","char_start":8708,"char_end":8767,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_047","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"Enable JavaScript to view this browser compatibility table.","location_hint":"paragraph 273","char_start":8805,"char_end":8864,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_048","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"In addition to the browser, the GPU itself also needs to support the feature. So, for example, S3 Texture Compression (S3TC) is only available on Tegra-based tablets. Most browsers make the WebGL context available through the webgl context name, but older ones need experimental-webgl as well. In addition, the upcoming WebGL 2 is fully backwards-compatible and will have the context name webgl2 .","location_hint":"paragraph 275","char_start":8895,"char_end":9292,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_049","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"Firefox provides two preferences available which let you control the capabilities of WebGL for testing purposes:","location_hint":"paragraph 278","char_start":9343,"char_end":9455,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_050","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"A Boolean property that, when true , enables a minimum capability mode. When in this mode, WebGL is configured to only support the bare minimum feature set and capabilities required by the WebGL specification. This lets you ensure that your WebGL code will work on any device or browser, regardless of their capabilities. This is false by default.","location_hint":"paragraph 280","char_start":9486,"char_end":9833,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_24107f739f88_051","source_id":"src_24107f739f88","source_hash":"16723d84e6799d70f3ed79ff67af576eaa1eeebe491ac0a16b79148c5fcd0086","text":"A Boolean property that, when true , disables all WebGL extensions. This is false by default.","location_hint":"paragraph 282","char_start":9863,"char_end":9956,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:45.768Z"}
